# The development profile, which is gitignored but sits on disk and would
# otherwise be compiled into the published jar. It carries R2 endpoint, key id
# and secret as literal defaults — described in the file as placeholders, but
# they are the shape of a credential and this image is pushed to a public
# registry. Deployment reads application-production.yml, which has no values in
# it at all, so nothing here needs the dev one.
#
# A consequence worth knowing: an image built with ENV=dev now starts on a
# profile whose configuration file is absent. That is the right trade — a dev
# image is not a thing you want; `mvn spring-boot:run -Pdev` is how you run
# locally.
src/main/resources/application-dev.yml

# Local tooling and anything env-shaped.
.env
.env.*
.claude/
.vscode/
